{"prompt_hash": "51c6bf114de86a702c3f7227bfbf5b42e92c642b1d4165adf2e9e988495003b1", "text": "Summary\nThis vegan mushroom risotto achieves a rich, creamy texture without dairy by leveraging the natural starches of Arborio rice and a technique called \"mantecatura\" using vegan fats. By slowly adding warm vegetable broth and stirring frequently, the rice releases amylopectin, creating a velvety sauce. Umami boosters like soy sauce or miso paste replace the depth usually provided by parmesan cheese.\n\nAssumptions\nI assume you have access to a heavy-bottomed pot or Dutch oven for even heat distribution and standard measuring tools.\n\nStructured Details\nIngredients Checklist:\n1.5 cups Arborio rice\n5-6 cups Vegetable broth (low sodium, kept simmering)\n1 lb Mixed mushrooms (cremini, shiitake, oyster), sliced\n1 Medium yellow onion, finely diced\n2 Cloves garlic, minced\n1/2 cup Dry white wine (Sauvignon Blanc or Pinot Grigio)\n3 tbsp Olive oil (divided)\n2 tbsp Vegan butter (cold)\n3 tbsp Nutritional yeast (essential for cheesy flavor)\n1 tbsp Soy sauce or white miso paste (for savory depth)\n1 tbsp Fresh thyme leaves\nSalt and black pepper to taste\nFresh parsley for garnish\n\nCooking Phases:\n\nOption 1: The Sauté & Toast | Flavor Foundation | High Heat\nStart by sautéing the mushrooms in 1 tbsp olive oil until browned and all liquid has evaporated; set them aside. In the same pot, add remaining oil and onions, cooking until translucent. Add the Arborio rice and toast for 2 minutes until edges are translucent. This toasting step ensures the grains hold their shape.\nAction: [Button: Watch Toasting Technique] https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=how+to+toast+risotto+rice\n\nOption 2: The Slow Simmer | Texture Development | Medium Heat\nDeglaze the pot with white wine and stir until fully absorbed. Begin adding the hot vegetable broth one ladle at a time. Stir almost constantly. Wait until the liquid is nearly absorbed before adding the next ladle. This friction releases the starch required for creaminess. Repeat this process for about 18-20 minutes until rice is al dente.\nAction: [Button: Risotto Stirring Tips] https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=risotto+stirring+technique\n\nOption 3: The Mantecatura | Creamy Finish | Heat Off\nRemove the pot from the heat immediately. This is crucial. Fold the cooked mushrooms back in. Add the cold vegan butter, nutritional yeast, and soy sauce/miso. Stir vigorously (whip it) for 1 minute to emulsify the fats with the starch. This creates the signature creamy wave. Season with salt, pepper, and fresh thyme.\nAction: [Button: Vegan Butter Options] https://www.google.com/search?q=best+vegan+butter+for+cooking\n\nOption 4: Plating & Serving | Presentation | Immediate\nServe immediately while the texture is loose and flowing (all'onda). Garnish with fresh parsley and a drizzle of high-quality olive oil. Risotto stiffens as it cools, so immediate service ensures the best texture.\nAction: [Button: Wine Pairing Guide] https://www.google.com/search?q=vegan+wine+pairing+mushroom+risotto\n\nImages\nCreamy Mushroom Risotto: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/mushroom-risotto\nArborio Rice Grains: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/arborio-rice\nFresh Herbs Prep: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/thyme-parsley\n\nIcons\nPrep Time: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/clock.svg\nServings: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/people.svg\nIngredients: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/basket.svg\n\nQuick Actions\nAction: [Button: Save to Recipe Box] https://www.google.com/search?q=save+recipe+app\nAction: [Button: Convert to Metric] https://www.google.com/search?q=cups+to+grams+converter\n\nSources\nSerious Eats (Vegan Risotto Science): https://www.seriouseats.com/vegan-risotto-recipe\nMinimalist Baker (Creamy Mushroom Risotto): https://minimalistbaker.com/creamy-vegetable-risotto-30-minutes/\nCookie and Kate (Mushroom Risot