{"prompt_hash": "21c2f985c038cd4e0e7545ec22b6ca97f06bb9bc6d831b843980adea125a723f", "text": "Summary\nThis vegan mushroom risotto achieves a rich, creamy texture without dairy by utilizing the high starch content of Arborio rice and a finishing technique called \"mantecatura.\" By incorporating nutritional yeast and soy sauce (or miso), the dish gains the savory umami depth typically provided by parmesan cheese. The key to success is keeping the vegetable broth hot and adding it gradually while stirring frequently to release the rice's amylopectin.\n\nAssumptions\nI assume you have a heavy-bottomed pot or Dutch oven for even heat distribution and standard measuring cups.\n\nStructured Details\nIngredients Overview\n| Ingredient | Amount | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Arborio Rice | 1.5 cups | Releases starch for creaminess |\n| Vegetable Broth | 5-6 cups | Warm liquid base (keep simmering) |\n| Mixed Mushrooms | 1 lb | Cremini, Shiitake, or Oyster (sliced) |\n| Dry White Wine | 1/2 cup | Acid and brightness (Sauvignon Blanc) |\n| Nutritional Yeast | 3 tbsp | Cheesy, savory flavor profile |\n| Vegan Butter | 2 tbsp | Cold cubes for finishing emulsion |\n| Umami Booster | 1 tbsp | Soy sauce or white miso paste |\n\nCooking Phases\n\nOption 1: The Base & Toast | Build flavor foundation | High Heat\nHeat olive oil in your pot. Sauté sliced mushrooms until browned and liquid evaporates, then remove them. Add diced onion to the pot, cook until translucent, then add minced garlic and Arborio rice. Toast the rice for 1-2 minutes until edges are translucent but centers remain opaque. This ensures the grains hold their structure.\nAction: [Button: Rice Toasting Visuals] https://www.google.com/search?q=how+to+toast+risotto+rice+visual+guide\n\nOption 2: Deglaze & Simmer | Release starch slowly | Medium Heat\nPour in the white wine and stir until fully evaporated. Begin adding the hot vegetable broth one ladle at a time. Stir frequently (every 30 seconds). Wait until the liquid is almost absorbed before adding the next ladle. Continue this process for 18-20 minutes until the rice is tender but has a slight bite (al dente).\nAction: [Button: Stirring Technique Video] https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=risotto+stirring+technique\n\nOption 3: The Mantecatura | Create creamy emulsion | Heat Off\nRemove pot from heat immediately. Stir in the cooked mushrooms, nutritional yeast, soy sauce, and cold vegan butter. Vigorously whip the mixture with a wooden spoon for 60 seconds. This agitation emulsifies the fat and starch into a thick, glossy sauce without any dairy.\nAction: [Button: Vegan Butter Brands] https://www.google.com/search?q=best+vegan+butter+for+risotto\n\nOption 4: Plating & Garnish | Serve at peak texture | Immediate\nServe instantly while the risotto creates a soft wave (all'onda) when the plate is tilted. Garnish with fresh thyme or parsley and plenty of cracked black pepper. If the risotto sits too long, it will stiffen, so timing is critical.\nAction: [Button: Wine Pairing Ideas] https://www.google.com/search?q=white+wine+pairing+mushroom+risotto\n\nImages\nPlated Mushroom Risotto: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/mushroom-risotto\nArborio Rice: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/arborio-rice\nSautéed Mushrooms: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/cooked-mushrooms\n\nIcons\nPrep Time: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/stopwatch.svg\nServings: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/people-fill.svg\nCooking Heat: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/fire.svg\n\nQuick Actions\nAction: [Button: Save Recipe] https://www.google.com/search?q=save+vegan+risotto+recipe\nAction: [Button: Metric Converter] https://www.google.com/search?q=cups+to+grams+converter\n\nSources\nSerious Eats (The Science of Risotto): https://www.seriouseats.com/how-to-make-perfect-risotto-recipe\nMinimalist Baker (Vegan Mushroom Risotto): https://minimalistbaker.com/creamy-vegetable-ris