etable broth one ladle (approx 1/2 cup) at a time. Stir frequently to agitate the rice grains against each other—this releases the starch. Wait until the liquid is mostly absorbed before adding the next ladle. Repeat for 18-20 minutes until rice is al dente.\nAction: [Button: Stirring Technique] https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=risotto+stirring+technique\n\nPhase 3: The Mantecatura | Create emulsion | Heat Off\nRemove the pot from the heat immediately. This is crucial. Stir in the cooked mushrooms, nutritional yeast, soy sauce (or miso), and the cold vegan butter. Whip the mixture vigorously with a wooden spoon for 60 seconds. The agitation combines the starch and fat into a glossy, creamy sauce.\nAction: [Button: Vegan Butter Brands] https://www.google.com/search?q=best+vegan+butter+for+cooking\n\nPhase 4: Plating | Serve immediately | Warm\nCheck seasoning and add salt/pepper. The consistency should be \"all'onda\" (wavy)—it should flow slowly when the plate is tilted, not stand stiff like mashed potatoes. Garnish with fresh parsley or thyme.\nAction: [Button: Plating Ideas] https://www.google.com/search?q=gourmet+risotto+plating+ideas\n\nImages\nCreamy Mushroom Risotto: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/mushroom_risotto\nArborio Rice Grains: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/arborio_rice\nCooking Process: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/cooking_risotto\n\nIcons\nPrep Time: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/clock-history.svg\nIngredients: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/basket2.svg\nCooking Heat: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/fire.svg\n\nQuick Actions\nAction: [Button: Save Recipe] https://www.google.com/search?q=bookmark+vegan+risotto+recipe\nAction: [Button: Find Vegan Wines] https://www.barnivore.com/\n\nSources\nSerious Eats (Science of Risotto): https://www.seriouseats.com/how-to-make-perfect-risotto-recipe\nMinimalist Baker (Vegan Risotto): https://minimalistbaker.com/cr