{"prompt_hash": "ebc49510a824a4bf54a9f7329241dd9fdaf14966faa9f6e227b4d0d111089245", "text": "London October Weather and Packing Essentials\nThree-Day Forecast Overview\nOctober 15-17 in London features cool temperatures (10-14°C) with heavy rain on day 1, strong winds on day 2, and partly cloudy conditions on day 3, demanding waterproof, wind-resistant, layerable clothing suitable for business meetings and urban walking.[1][2][3]\n\nTrip Context\nThis packing list assumes a business trip with daily meetings, some outdoor travel via walking or public transport, moderate luggage (carry-on friendly), and a focus on versatile, professional attire in neutral tones like black or grey to match London style. Footwear prioritizes comfort for wet/windy conditions; outerwear emphasizes rain and wind protection.[1][2][4]\n\nTailored Three-Day Packing List\nCore Clothing (layer for 10-14°C variability):\n- 3 long-sleeve shirts or blouses (breathable cotton or merino for layering under jackets).[2][3]\n- 2 sweaters or cardigans (light wool or cashmere for warmth during wind/rain).[1][4]\n- 2 pairs trousers (jeans or ponte pants, quick-dry black for business casual).[1][2]\n- 1 button-up shirt or blouse for meetings.\n- 3-5 underwear, 3 socks, 1 sleep set.\n\nOuterwear (essential for rain/wind):\n- Stylish waterproof raincoat or trench coat (hooded, packable for heavy rain and wind).[1][2][4]\n- Light leather or windproof jacket as backup layer.\n- Compact umbrella (wind-resistant).\n- Scarf and beanie for chilly evenings.[1][3]\n\nFootwear (practical, stylish for business):\n- Waterproof ankle boots or leather walking shoes (suede or rubber-soled for rain/wind grip).[1][4]\n- 1 pair loafers or flats for indoor meetings (water-resistant if possible).\n\nAccessories:\n- Crossbody or anti-theft bag for laptop/documents/phone.[1][2]\n- Thin long underwear or thermals as base layer if sensitive to cold.[5]\n\nDay-by-Day Outfit Guide Table\n| Day | Weather | Suggested Outfit | Footwear | Outerwear |\n|-----|---------|------------------|----------|-----------|\n| Oct 15 | 12°C, Heavy Rain | Long-sleeve shirt + trousers + sweater | Waterproof boots | Raincoat + umbrella |\n| Oct 16 | 10°C, Strong Winds | Button-up + jeans + cardigan | Ankle boots (grippy sole) | Trench coat + scarf |\n| Oct 17 | 14°C, Partly Cloudy | Blouse + trousers + light sweater | Loafers or flats | Light jacket + beanie |\n\nImages:\nLondon Rainy Street: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/london,rain\nAutumn London Walk: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/london,autumn\nWindy Thames: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/london,windy\n\nIcons:\numbrella: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/umbrella-fill.svg\nwind: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/wind.svg\nraincoat: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/rain-heavy.svg\n\nQuick Actions\nAction: [Button: View Full Autumn Guide] https://nordace.com/en/what-to-wear-in-london-in-autumn-packing-list/\nAction: [Button: Shop Raincoats] https://www.travelfashiongirl.com/what-to-pack-for-london-on-your-trip-to-the-united-kingdom/\n\nSources\nhttps://nordace.com/en/what-to-wear-in-london-in-autumn-packing-list/[1]\nhttps://www.travelfashiongirl.com/what-to-pack-for-london-on-your-trip-to-the-united-kingdom/[2]\nhttps://knackbags.com/blogs/one-bag-blog/ultimate-london-packing-guide-what-to-bring-for-every-season[4]", "raw": {"id": "ce30400a-f081-4fc6-b172-e7cf3cbd8cfa", "model": "sonar-pro", "created": 1771343058, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1135, "completion_tokens": 869, "total_tokens": 2004, "search_context_size": "low", "cost": {"input_tokens_cost": 0.00341, "output_tokens_cost": 0.01303, "request_cost": 0.006, "total_cost": 0.02244}}, "citations": ["https://nordace.com/en/what-to-wear-in-london-in-autumn-packing-list/", "https://www.travelfashiongirl.com/what-to-pack-for-london-on-your-trip-to-the-united-kingdom/", "https://www.aladyinlondon.com/2025/09/london-autumn-packing-l