{"prompt_hash": "4e36c9a1c912ba125df24805816e9299c3d73cd283978a9d40e385bbd8f951b2", "text": "# Mobile Application Development Timeline: November 2024 - February 2025\n\n## Project Overview and Duration\n\nThis 16-week mobile application development project spans from November 1, 2024 to February 15, 2025, encompassing four primary phases: UI/UX design, frontend development, backend integration, and QA testing. The timeline allocates resources across these phases with three-week milestone checkpoints to ensure consistent progress tracking and stakeholder alignment.\n\n## Context and Assumptions\n\nThis timeline assumes a standard mobile app development approach with the following parameters:\n\n- Team composition includes UI/UX designers, frontend developers, backend engineers, and QA specialists working in parallel where dependencies allow\n- The project follows a phased approach where UI/UX design completion gates frontend development initiation\n- Backend integration occurs concurrently with frontend development after initial architecture planning\n- QA testing includes feature testing at each demo cycle and end-to-end testing before launch\n- Each three-week milestone represents a formal review and decision point for phase progression\n- No extended team unavailability or external blockers are anticipated\n- The project maintains a single mobile platform focus (iOS or Android) to streamline development\n\n## Detailed Project Timeline with Milestones\n\nPHASE 1: UI/UX DESIGN (Weeks 1-4)\n\nWeek 1-3 (November 1 - November 21, 2024)\nMilestone 1 (November 21): Requirements documentation complete, design kickoff approved\nActivities: Gather app requirements, define user personas, map user workflows, establish design system foundations\nDeliverables: Requirements specification document, user journey maps, initial wireframes\n\nWeek 4-6 (November 22 - December 12, 2024)\nMilestone 2 (December 12): High-fidelity designs approved for development handoff\nActivities: Create high-fidelity mockups, conduct design reviews, incorporate stakeholder feedback, prepare design specifications\nDeliverables: Complete design system, UI mockups for all screens, design specifications document\n\nPHASE 2: FRONTEND DEVELOPMENT (Weeks 5-12)\n\nWeek 7-9 (December 13 - January 2, 2025)\nMilestone 3 (January 2): Core UI components built and integrated\nActivities: Set up development environment, build reusable UI components, implement navigation structure, integrate design system\nDeliverables: Component library, navigation framework, initial app screens\n\nWeek 10-12 (January 3 - January 23, 2025)\nMilestone 4 (January 23): Frontend feature implementation 75% complete\nActivities: Build remaining feature screens, implement user interactions, integrate state management, conduct code reviews\nDeliverables: Functional frontend with 75% feature coverage, code repository with version control\n\nWeek 13-15 (January 24 - February 13, 2025)\nMilestone 5 (February 13): Frontend development complete, ready for backend integration testing\nActivities: Complete remaining features, optimize performance, conduct internal frontend testing, prepare for integration\nDeliverables: Complete frontend codebase, performance optimization report\n\nPHASE 3: BACKEND INTEGRATION (Weeks 7-14)\n\nWeek 7-9 (December 13 - January 2, 2025)\nMilestone 3 (January 2): API architecture and specifications finalized\nActivities: Design API endpoints, plan database schema, establish authentication framework, prepare integration documentation\nDeliverables: API specification document, database design, authentication architecture\n\nWeek 10-12 (January 3 - January 23, 2025)\nMilestone 4 (January 23): Core backend services deployed and tested\nActivities: Develop API endpoints, implement database operations, set up backend infrastructure, conduct API testing\nDeliverables: Functional API endpoints, database implementation, backend testing report\n\nWeek 13-15 (January 24 - February 13, 2025)\nMilestone 5 (February 13): Frontend-backend integration complete and functional\nActivities: Integrate frontend with backend services, test data flow, resolve integration issues, optimize communication\nDeliverables: Integrated system, integration testing report, resolved issue log\n\nPHASE 4: QA TESTING (Weeks 13-16)\n\nWeek 13-15 (January 24 - February 13, 2025)\nMilestone 5 (February 13): Feature testing complete, critical issues resolved\nActivities: Execute feature test cases, perform regression testing, document defects, verify fixes\nDeliverables: Feature test report, defect log, resolved issues\n\nWeek 16 (February 14 - February 15, 2025)\nMilestone 6 (February 15): End-to-end testing complete, app ready for launch\nActivities: Conduct end-to-end system testing, perform final smoke testing, validate all user workflows, prepare release notes\nDeliverables: End-to-end test report, release notes, launch readiness sign-off\n\n## Three-Week Milestone Summary Table\n\nMilestone | Date | Phase | Key Deliverable | Status Gate\n---|---|---|---|---\nMilestone 1 | November 21, 2024 | UI/UX Design | Requirements and initial designs approved | Proceed to detailed design\nMilestone 2 | December 12, 2024 | UI/UX Design | High-fidelity designs finalized | Development handoff approved\nMilestone 3 | January 2, 2025 | Frontend/Backend | Components built, APIs specified | Development ramp-up\nMilestone 4 | January 23, 2025 | Frontend/Backend | 75% features complete, core services deployed | Integration phase\nMilestone 5 | February 13, 2025 | Frontend/Backend/QA | Integration complete, feature testing done | Final QA phase\nMilestone 6 | February 15, 2025 | QA Testing | End-to-end testing complete | Launch ready\n\n## Quick Actions\n\n- Establish project kickoff meeting for November 1 to align team on requirements and timeline\n- Schedule design review sessions every two weeks during UI/UX phase\n- Set up development environment and repository access before December 13\n- Plan integration testing logistics by January 15\n- Prepare launch checklist and deployment procedures by February 10\n\n## Resource Allocation Notes\n\nUI/UX Design: 2-3 designers (Weeks 1-6, reduced involvement thereafter for refinements)\nFrontend Development: 2-3 developers (Weeks 5-15, peak capacity Weeks 10-15)\nBackend Development: 2-3 engineers (Weeks 7-15, peak capacity Weeks 10-15)\nQA Testing: 2 QA specialists (Weeks 13-16, with overlap starting Week 13)\nProject Manager: 1 full-time coordinator (Weeks 1-16)", "raw": {"id": "6f13fe0d-6a41-44c5-ba6d-04f2a41125b2", "model": "sonar-pro", "created": 1771343188, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1111, "completion_tokens": 1405, "total_tokens": 2516, "search_context_size": "low", "cost": {"input_tokens_cost": 0.00333, "output_tokens_cost": 0.02107, "request_cost": 0.006, "total_cost": 0.03041}}, "citations": ["https://soltech.net/whats-timeline-building-mobile-app/", "https://miro.com/templates/timeline-project-timeline/", "https://www.cascade.app/google-sheet-templates/app-development-plan-template", "https://www.smartsheet.com/content/project-timeline-templates", "https://www.goodday.work/templates/mobile-application", "https://excel.cloud.microsoft/create/en/timeline-templates/", "https://www.tomsplanner.com/templates/mobile-application-development/", "https://www.canva.com/templates/s/timeline/", "https://www.template.net/edit-online/391847/mobile-app-development-timeline"], "search_results": [{"title": "Mobile App Development Timeline: What You Can Expect - soltech", "url": "https://soltech.net/whats-timeline-building-mobile-app/", "date": "2025-06-26", "last_updated": "2026-02-17", "snippet": "Mobile App Requirements & Design: 2-4 weeks · Mobile App Planning: 1-2 Weeks · Mobile App Development: 3-6 Months · Mobile App Testing: 3-6 weeks.", "source": "web"}, {"title": "FREE Project Timeline Template | Product Development Planning", "url": "https://miro.com/templates/timeline-project-timeline/", "date": "2025-08-13"