{"prompt_hash": "2ef9e62a0520b25b634ff4936466d1669d8df408639f6fd9832c15e417a721cc", "text": "Traditional Ragù alla Bolognese for 4\n\nRecipe Background\nThis recipe draws from authentic sources like the Accademia Italiana della Cucina and Italian home cooks, scaled to serve 4 with a classic soffritto base, dual meats, milk for tenderness, and a 3-hour slow simmer for deep flavor. It yields about 1.2 kg sauce, enough for 400g dried tagliatelle.\n\nMetric Ingredients List\n300g coarsely ground beef (70-80% lean)\n300g ground pork\n50g pancetta, finely diced\n1 medium onion (150g), finely diced\n1 medium carrot (100g), finely diced\n1 celery stalk (80g), finely diced\n2 tbsp (30ml) olive oil\n50ml dry white wine (or red)\n2 tbsp (50g) tomato paste\n400ml tomato passata (or puree)\n100ml whole milk\n1 bay leaf\nSalt and black pepper to taste\nPinch of nutmeg (optional)\n\n3-Hour Slow Simmer Steps\n1. In a large heavy pot over low heat, add olive oil and pancetta. Render fat for 5 minutes until crisp, no browning.\n2. Add diced onion, carrot, and celery (soffritto). Cook covered on low for 10-15 minutes until soft and translucent, stirring occasionally.\n3. Increase to medium heat. Add beef and pork, breaking up with a spoon. Cook 10 minutes until meat loses raw color and starts browning, seasoning lightly with salt and pepper. Drain excess fat if needed.\n4. Pour in white wine. Simmer on high until fully evaporated, about 2-3 minutes.\n5. Stir in tomato paste, cooking 2 minutes to caramelize. Add passata, bay leaf, and nutmeg. Bring to a gentle boil.\n6. Reduce to lowest heat, cover partially, and simmer 3 hours. Stir every 20-30 minutes; add a splash of water (20ml) if too thick. Sauce should reduce to thick, velvety consistency with fat separating slightly.\n7. In last 15 minutes, stir in milk. Simmer uncovered, stirring often, until absorbed and silky. Remove bay leaf. Taste and adjust salt/pepper.\n8. Serve with cooked tagliatelle, grated Parmigiano-Reggiano.\n\nCooking Tips\nUse a heavy Dutch oven for even low heat. Total time: 3.5 hours. Freezes well up to 3 months. Pairs best with egg pasta, not spaghetti.\n\nImages:\nClassic Ragù alla Bolognese: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/bolognese-sauce\nSoffritto Prep: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/italian-soffritto\nSlow Simmer Pot: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/ragu-simmering\n\nIcons:\npasta: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/pasta.svg\nfire: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/fire.svg\nclock: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/clock.svg\n\nQuick Actions\nPairing Guide: https://www.eataly.com/us_en/magazine/how-to/pasta-perfect-pairings/\nPasta Buying: https://www.amazon.com/s?k=dried+tagliatelle\n\nSources\nhttps://anitalianinmykitchen.com/bolognese-sauce/\nhttps://www.accademiaitalianadellacucina.it/sites/default/files/Rag%C3%B9%20alla%20bolognese%20-%20updated%20recipe_20%20April%202023.pdf\nhttps://leitesculinaria.com/84057/recipes-marcella-hazan-bolognese-sauce.html", "raw": {"id": "0a93b1b7-3af1-4435-b111-f2f9a5dd76fe", "model": "sonar-pro", "created": 1771343207, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1099, "completion_tokens": 825, "total_tokens": 1924, "search_context_size": "low", "cost": {"input_tokens_cost": 0.0033, "output_tokens_cost": 0.01238, "request_cost": 0.006, "total_cost": 0.02167}}, "citations": ["https://anitalianinmykitchen.com/bolognese-sauce/", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hzKqYgUp_ww", "https://ohsweetbasil.com/the-secret-to-authentic-italian-bolognese-sauce-recipe/", "https://leitesculinaria.com/84057/recipes-marcella-hazan-bolognese-sauce.html", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QVVkHc1Qz2A", "https://vikalinka.com/spaghetti-bolognese/", "https://www.accademiaitalianadellacucina.it/sites/default/files/Rag%C3%B9%20alla%20bolognese%20-%20updated%20recipe_20%20April%202023.pdf"], "search_results": [{"title": "Authentic Bolognese Sauce Recipe - An Italian in my Kitchen", "url": "https://