{"prompt_hash": "957035594b7a2e7919458094a25ac34be526bba44ec0a8ce159cb5197b5e431d", "text": "Neo-Tokyo Data Courier Protagonist Profile\n\nCyberpunk Creation Context\nDrawing from Cyberpunk 2020 and Red character sheet templates, this profile uses standard elements like name, handle, role, cyberware, and lifepath for a freelance data courier in a neon-drenched Neo-Tokyo. Assumes a gritty 2040s setting blending Tokyo's sprawl with cyberpunk tropes: megacorp towers, street syndicates, and black-market chrome.[1][2]\n\nCore Character Sheet\nName: Kira \"Ghostwire\" Sato  \nAge: 28  \nPhysical Description: Lean 5'6\" frame, wiry build at 125 lbs, pale skin scarred by low-end chrome interfaces, short asymmetrical black hair with glowing blue fiber-optic streaks, one natural brown eye and one cybernetic red optic with HUD overlay, tattooed yakuza-style circuits crawling up her neck, dressed in layered synth-leather jacket, cargo pants, and mag-locked boots for urban traversal.  \nUnique Cybernetic Enhancement: Neural Ghostwire Implant - a black-market spinal lace allowing direct brain-to-datajack wireless transfer of encrypted payloads at 10x standard speeds, with ghosting mode to spoof ICE (Intrusion Countermeasures Electronics) traces for 30 seconds; risks neural burnout on overuse.[2]  \nOccupation: Freelance data courier, dodging corp sec and rival runners to deliver high-risk digital payloads across Neo-Tokyo's undergrid.\n\nDebt Backstory (312 words)\nKira grew up in the rain-slicked gutters of Neo-Tokyo's Shibuya sprawl, daughter of a burned-out netrunner dad who fried his brain chasing corpo secrets and a street-doc mom who patched gangers for eddies. At 16, she jacked her first deck, hustling small gigs smuggling pirated code for fixers. Talent caught the eye of the Black Lotus syndicate, yakuza heirs dominating the shadow net. They fronted her the Ghostwire implant - experimental chrome smuggled from Arasaka labs - turning her into their golden ghost, running payloads no one else could touch.\n\nPeak came at 25: a 2-million-eddie score delivering biotech schematics from a Mitsuhama exec's cranial vault. But the run glitched. Rival Tyger Claws hacked her ghosting mode mid-job, pinning the heist on her. Mitsuhama bounties hit, Lotus enforcers assumed betrayal. Kira bolted, but the implant's kill-switch firmware activated - a syndicate backdoor she never saw coming. It wiped her savings, locked her accounts, and tagged her with a 1.2-million-eddie debt for \"stolen assets and disloyalty.\"\n\nNow, three years deep in the sprawl's underbelly, Kira runs freelance for anyone paying: solos, media, even rival syndicates. Every gig chips at the debt, but Lotus collectors lurk - ink-skinned oyabun sending razor-limbed ninjas to collect interest in blood. Ghostwire saves her ass, letting her phase through firewalls and drone swarms, but each burnout spikes migraines, whispering syndicate overrides in her skull. Survival means outrunning the neon noose: one big score to buy a black-market scrubber for the implant, or become another gutter ghost. Neo-Tokyo chews dreamers; Kira's just fighting to not be next.[1][2]\n\nVisual Assets for Cyberpunk Vibe\nImages:  \nNeo-Tokyo Courier Portrait: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/cyberpunk-runner  \nChrome Implant Closeup: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/cybernetic-spine  \nSprawl Night Chase: https://loremflickr.com/1200/800/neon-city-chase  \nIcons:  \nDatajack: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/cpu.svg  \nNeural Link: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/brain.svg  \nDebt Tracker: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/icons/currency-exchange.svg\n\nCharacter Sheet Reference Links\nBlank Cyberpunk 2020 Sheet: https://www.scribd.com/document/450158626/Blank-Cyberpunk-2020-Character-Sheet-pdf[1]  \nCyberpunk Red Creation Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fe0dix_FDMQ[2]  \nOnline Generator: https://cp2020-char-creator.herokuapp.com