{"prompt_hash": "a68fd181972e7edc95440880984950d7da02ec22c119bb4e7a12e8319f8728c6", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"surface-prague-clockmaker\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\",\n      \"theme\": {\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#8B4513\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"updateComponents\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"surface-prague-clockmaker\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"title\",\n            \"divider1\",\n            \"header_context\",\n            \"body_context\",\n            \"header_tale\",\n            \"body_tale_1\",\n            \"body_tale_2\",\n            \"header_accident\",\n            \"body_accident_1\",\n            \"body_accident_2\",\n            \"header_shadow\",\n            \"body_shadow_1\",\n            \"body_shadow_2\",\n            \"divider2\",\n            \"header_extensions\",\n            \"list_extensions\",\n            \"divider3\",\n            \"header_sources\",\n            \"list_sources\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Prague Clockmaker's Timeless Discovery\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"divider1\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_context\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Historical and Cultural Context\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_context\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"In 1895 Prague, clockmakers like Ludvík Hainz and Romuald Božek were active, maintaining intricate timepieces amid the city's legacy of horology, including the famous Astronomical Clock (Orloj) installed in 1410 by Mikuláš of Kadaň.[1][2] This era blended artisanal craftsmanship with emerging industrial influences, set against the cobblestone streets of the Old Town.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_tale\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Watchmaker's Tale\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_tale_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"In the dim glow of oil lamps, František Novák hunched over his workbench in a narrow shop on Jilská Street, Prague, 1895. The air hummed with the ticking symphony of brass gears and pendulums, remnants of his trade in an age when time governed empires. František, a wiry man of 52 with ink-stained fingers and spectacles perpetually fogged, had inherited the shop from his father, a disciple of the legendary Hanuš, whose blinded eyes haunted local legends.[1][5]\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_tale_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"One autumn evening, as gaslight flickered through frost-laced windows, František unpacked a dusty velvet pouch from an anonymous estate sale. Inside nestled a pocket watch unlike any other: silver-cased, its face etched with alchemical symbols—a sun, moon, and cryptic zodiac wheel. The mechanism whirred with unnatural silence, its single hand frozen at XII. Curiosity piqued, he wound it. A faint vibration coursed through his palm, and the room... stilled.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_accident\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Accident Averted\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_accident_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The next morning, chaos erupted in the crowded shop. A boisterous apprentice, young Karel, juggled a tray of delicate hourglass components while reaching for a ladder to dust high shelves. Tourists milled about, admiring turret clock models inspired by the Orloj.[2] In a split second, Karel's foot slipped; the ladder teetered, sending the tray airborne toward a cluster of porcelain-faced clocks below. Shards seemed inevitable—ruin for František's livelihood.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_accident_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"His hand dove into his vest. Fingers closed on the watch. He pressed the hidden crown. Time halted. Dust motes hung mid-air like stars arrested in orbit. The tray floated, inches from disaster; Karel's eyes widened in perpetual surprise. Five seconds—an eternity in stillness. František sidestepped, plucked the tray from suspension, steadied the ladder, and repositioned Karel safely. With a click, time resumed. The ladder wobbled innocently; the tray settled harmlessly. Karel blinked, muttering, \\\"Slipped again, master?\\\" František smiled faintly, heart pounding. \\\"Careful, boy. Time waits for no one.\\\"\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_shadow\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Secret's Shadow\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_shadow_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Word of the watch spread in whispers among horologists, but František guarded it fiercely. He tested it sparingly: once to savor a stolen glance at a passing noblewoman, her parasol twirling eternally; another to evade a pickpocket in Staroměstské náměstí. Yet power corrupted subtly. Five seconds blurred into temptation—delaying a creditor's knock, glimpsing rivals' designs. By winter's end, the watch's glow dimmed, its hand inching past XII. František dismantled it one stormy night, gears dissolving into inert metal. \\\"Some mechanisms,\\\" he murmured, \\\"defy their makers.\\\"\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"body_shadow_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"In his final years, he crafted replicas of the Orloj for tourists, weaving the tale as folklore. Prague's clocks ticked on, oblivious, as František Novák faded into legend—a man who held time, if only briefly, in his palm.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"divider2\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_extensions\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Prague Clockmaker Extensions\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"list_extensions\",\n          \"component\": \"List\",\n          \"direction\": \"vertical\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"ext_item_1\",\n            \"ext_item_2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ext_item_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"• Expand to novella: Add Habsburg intrigue and Orloj sabotage plot.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ext_item_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"• Visual inspirations: Sketches of 1895 workshops or the magical watch.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"divider3\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_sources\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Sources\",\n          \"variant\": \"h4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"list_sources\",\n          \"component\": \"List\",\n          \"direction\": \"vertical\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"src_btn_1\",\n            \"src_btn_2\",\n            \"src_btn_3\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n    