: \"mediumFeature\",\n          \"fit\": \"cover\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_1_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\",\n          \"text\": \"Blade Runner\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_1_meta\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"caption\",\n          \"text\": \"Director: Ridley Scott (1982)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_1_desc\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\",\n          \"text\": \"High Tech, Low Life: This film defines the theme with its vision of 2019 Los Angeles. Towering neon skyscrapers and flying cars ('spinners') represent the high tech, while the perpetually rainy, grimy, and overcrowded streets show the low life. Advanced bio-engineered androids ('replicants') are hunted down in a society where technological marvels coexist with urban decay and a profound loss of humanity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"film_2_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"film_2_image\",\n            \"film_2_title\",\n            \"film_2_meta\",\n            \"film_2_desc\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_image\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": \"/images/akira_poster.jpg\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\",\n          \"fit\": \"cover\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\",\n          \"text\": \"Akira (Japanese)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_meta\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"caption\",\n          \"text\": \"Director: Katsuhiro Otomo (1988)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_2_desc\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\",\n          \"text\": \"High Tech, Low Life: Set in the sprawling metropolis of Neo-Tokyo, the film showcases incredible technology, from futuristic motorcycles to secret government psychic energy projects. This is contrasted with a society on the verge of collapse, depicted through violent biker gangs, anti-government terrorists, corrupt politicians, and a disenfranchised youth rebelling in the decaying, neon-drenched urban landscape.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"film_3_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"film_3_image\",\n            \"film_3_title\",\n            \"film_3_meta\",\n            \"film_3_desc\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_image\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": \"/images/ghost_in_the_shell_poster.jpg\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\",\n          \"fit\": \"cover\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\",\n          \"text\": \"Ghost in the Shell (Japanese)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_meta\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"caption\",\n          \"text\": \"Director: Mamoru Oshii (1995)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_3_desc\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\",\n          \"text\": \"High Tech, Low Life: In a future where full-body cybernetic prosthetics are commonplace, the 'high tech' is the seamless integration of humanity and machine. The 'low life' is explored through the dark underbelly this creates: cyber-crime, 'ghost-hacking' (taking control of someone's mind), and a pervasive sense of identity loss as characters question their own humanity in a world where memories can be altered and bodies are disposable shells.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"film_4_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"film_4_image\",\n            \"film_4_title\",\n            \"film_4_meta\",\n            \"film_4_desc\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_image\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": \"/images/strange_days_poster.jpg\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\",\n          \"fit\": \"cover\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\",\n          \"text\": \"Strange Days\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_meta\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"caption\",\n          \"text\": \"Director: Kathryn Bigelow (1995)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_4_desc\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\",\n          \"text\": \"High Tech, Low Life: The high-tech element is the 'SQUID', an illegal device that records experiences directly from the cerebral cortex for others to relive. The low-life aspect is the black market that thrives on these recordings, particularly illicit and violent ones. The protagonist is a hustler dealing these dangerous \\\"clips\\\" in a chaotic, pre-millennium Los Angeles rife with social tension, crime, and police corruption.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"film_5_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"film_5_image\",\n            \"film_5_title\",\n            \"film_5_meta\",\n            \"film_5_desc\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_image\",\n          \"component\": \"Image\",\n          \"url\": \"/images/the_matrix_poster.jpg\",\n          \"variant\": \"mediumFeature\",\n          \"fit\": \"cover\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"h3\",\n          \"text\": \"The Matrix\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_meta\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"caption\",\n          \"text\": \"Director: The Wachowskis (1999)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"film_5_desc\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\",\n          \"text\": \"High Tech, Low Life: This film presents the ultimate 'high tech, low life' scenario. The high tech is the Matrix itself, a flawless simulated reality that has imprisoned humanity. The 'low life' is the grim truth: humans are nothing more than a bio-electric power source for intelligent machines, and the few who have escaped live a desperate existence in the desolate, machine-controlled ruins of the real world.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"actions_section\",\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"justify\": \"start\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"btn_trailers\",\n            \"btn_explore\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"btn_trailers\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"variant\": \"primary\",\n          \"child\": \"txt_trailers\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"functionCall\": {\n              \"call\": \"openUrl\",\n              \"args\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=classic+cyberpunk+movie+trailers\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"txt_trailers\",\n          \"component\": \"T