{"prompt_hash": "0002282c47eff15aa467c5d28a029f16d6a7e62457b743fad97fa22c0b16de6a", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"story-surface-001\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\",\n      \"theme\": {\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#8B4513\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"updateComponents\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"story-surface-001\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"header\",\n            \"divider\",\n            \"story_content\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Clockmaker's Five Seconds\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"divider\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"story_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"para_1\",\n            \"para_2\",\n            \"para_3\",\n            \"para_4\",\n            \"para_5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"para_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Josef Kovář, a man whose hands moved with the precision of the gears he meticulously crafted, owned a small, unassuming clock shop nestled in the labyrinthine alleys of Prague in the year 1895. His shop, \\\"Časové Kouzlo\\\" (Time's Magic), was a sanctuary of ticking, chiming, and the gentle whir of unseen mechanisms. Josef, a bachelor in his late forties, lived for the intricate dance of springs and cogs.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"para_2\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"One crisp autumn evening, while disassembling an antique pocket watch brought in by a reclusive count, Josef discovered a peculiar additional mechanism. It was a tiny, almost invisible lever, connected to a crystal that pulsed with a faint, otherworldly blue light when activated. Driven by an insatiable curiosity, Josef spent weeks studying it, sacrificing sleep and meals. Finally, with a trembling hand, he pressed the lever.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"para_3\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The world around him froze. The pendulum of the grandfather clock in the corner hung mid-swing, a dust motes suspended in the air like tiny, frozen stars, and the distant clatter of a horse-drawn carriage from outside vanished into an absolute silence. Josef, however, could move freely. He checked his own pocket watch – exactly five seconds had passed when the world snapped back into motion, the pendulum resuming its swing with a soft 'tick-tock', the dust motes falling, and the carriage sound returning. He had stumbled upon a device that could halt time itself, for precisely five seconds. He named it the \\\"Chronos Shard.\\\"\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"para_4\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"A week later, the Chronos Shard found its purpose. Josef was perched precariously on a tall stool, reaching for a rare, gilded cuckoo clock on a high shelf. Below him, his young apprentice, Karel, was meticulously polishing a display case filled with delicate porcelain figurines. As Josef stretched, his elbow accidentally nudged a stack of finely crafted wooden gears he had left on the edge of his workbench. They teetered, threatening to cascade down onto Karel and the fragile porcelain below. A scream caught in Karel's throat as he looked up, eyes wide with horror.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"para_5\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Without a moment's hesitation, Josef's hand flew to his waistcoat pocket, retrieving the Chronos Shard. He pressed the lever. The world immediately plunged into silence and stillness. Karel was frozen, one hand reaching out in a futile attempt to catch the falling gears. Josef moved with practiced haste, stepping off the stool, gently intercepting the gears mid-air, and placing them safely back on the workbench. He then subtly nudged Karel's polishing cloth a fraction of an inch further, making it appear as though the apprentice had simply paused in his work. Five seconds later, the world resumed. The gears were safe, Karel blinked, looking confused, and Josef merely cleared his throat. \\\"Careful there, Karel,\\\" he said, feigning a slight wobble as he descended the stool, \\\"almost had a tumble.\\\" Karel, still a little pale, nodded, none the wiser, and continued polishing, oblivious to the near disaster, or the silent, five-second miracle that had just occurred. Josef merely smiled, a secret keeper of time's brief pause, in the heart of old Prague.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "[\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"story-surface-001\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\",\n      \"theme\": {\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#8B4513\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\",\n    \"updateComponents\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"story-surface-001\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"header\",\n            \"divider\",\n            \"story_content\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Clockmaker's Five Seconds\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\