{"prompt_hash": "64296c27c34905df709ab8c68baab7319222f59b403aa4075796acd415b78dca", "text": "[\n  {\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"celestial-express-mystery\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\",\n      \"theme\": {\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#1A237E\",\n        \"agentDisplayName\": \"Mystery Writer\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"updateComponents\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"celestial-express-mystery\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"header_title\",\n            \"assumptions_text\",\n            \"divider_1\",\n            \"section_setting_title\",\n            \"section_setting_body\",\n            \"section_victim_title\",\n            \"section_victim_body\",\n            \"section_weapon_title\",\n            \"section_weapon_body\",\n            \"section_suspects_title\",\n            \"suspect_1_card\",\n            \"suspect_2_card\",\n            \"suspect_3_card\",\n            \"section_twist_title\",\n            \"section_twist_body\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"header_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Celestial Express Mystery\",\n          \"variant\": \"h1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"assumptions_text\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Assumptions: The luxury train is a fictional service, \\\"The Celestial Express,\\\" renowned for its opulent design and exclusive clientele, traveling through Europe in 1935. The murder takes place discreetly within one of the private compartments.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"divider_1\",\n          \"component\": \"Divider\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_setting_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Setting\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_setting_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The year is 1935. The journey unfolds aboard \\\"The Celestial Express,\\\" a lavish, trans-European luxury train, as it makes its celebrated five-day voyage from the Gare de Lyon in Paris to the Sirkeci Terminal in Istanbul. The train is a moving palace of polished wood, brass, and velvet, filled with an eclectic mix of European aristocracy, industrialists, artists, and spies, all confined within its luxurious carriages as it speeds across picturesque landscapes and through bustling cities.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_victim_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Victim\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_victim_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Baroness Eleanor Dubois. A formidable and famously ruthless French industrialist, known for her sharp wit, scandalous past, and a reputation for crushing rivals without mercy. She is found dead in her lavish private compartment, appearing to have died peacefully in her sleep. However, a closer inspection reveals a tiny, almost invisible puncture mark on her neck.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_weapon_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Murder Weapon\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_weapon_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"A small, poisoned hatpin. The pin, intricately decorated with a faux pearl, was custom-made and coated with a fast-acting, undetectable neurotoxin. It was likely administered during a brief, close encounter, leaving minimal evidence.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_suspects_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Suspects and Motives\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_1_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"suspect_1_col\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_1_col\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"suspect_1_title\",\n            \"suspect_1_body\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_1_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Suspect 1: Monsieur Antoine Dubois\",\n          \"variant\": \"h4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_1_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Motive: Financial Ruin and Revenge. Antoine is the Baroness's estranged nephew, recently disinherited after his failing art gallery was refused a crucial loan by his aunt. He is desperate, facing bankruptcy, and believes the Baroness deliberately sabotaged his attempts to secure funding, driven by her disdain for his lifestyle. He stands to inherit a substantial sum upon her death, despite the disinheritance, due to a clause in an older will.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_2_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"suspect_2_col\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_2_col\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"suspect_2_title\",\n            \"suspect_2_body\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_2_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Suspect 2: Lady Beatrice Finch\",\n          \"variant\": \"h4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_2_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Motive: Long-held Grudge and Social Retribution. Lady Beatrice is a seemingly demure English socialite whose prominent family suffered a devastating financial collapse years ago, directly attributable to a hostile takeover orchestrated by Baroness Dubois. Lady Beatrice's family was publicly shamed and impoverished, and she has carried a quiet, simmering resentment, seeking an opportunity for retribution against the woman who ruined her family's standing.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_3_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"suspect_3_col\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_3_col\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"suspect_3_title\",\n            \"suspect_3_body\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_3_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Suspect 3: Dr. Alistair Reed\",\n          \"variant\": \"h4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"suspect_3_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Motive: Professional Integrity and Protection of Legacy. Dr. Reed is a renowned British archaeologist traveling with a newly discovered, invaluable ancient artifact that the Baroness had publicly and aggressively attempted to acquire through highly questionable means. Her tactics threatened to discredit Dr. Reed's reputation and research, potentially leading to the artifact being seized and misused. He feared she would stop at nothing to possess it, even resorting to theft.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_twist_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The Plot Twist\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"section_twist_body\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"The true killer is Lady Beatrice Finch, but her primary motive is not personal revenge. Lady Beatrice is, in fact, an undercover agent for the British Secret Service. Baroness Dubois was secretly a key figure in an international espionage ring, planning to sell highly sensitive industrial and military secrets to a rival power during a clandestine meeting in Istanbul. Lady Beatrice was assigned to eliminate the Baroness and retrieve crucial documents hidden in the Baroness's compartment before the train reached its destination. Her family's historical grievance against the Baroness served as a perfect, believable cover for her presence and actions on the train, diverting suspicion from her true mission. The poisoned hatpin was a specialized tool developed by the Secret Service for discreet assassinations. The \\\"disinheritance\\\" of Monsieur Dubois and Dr. Reed's \\\"archaeological artifact\\\" were elaborate red herrings, carefully placed or exploited by Lady Beatrice to further obscure her real objective.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\"\n  }\n]", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "[\n  {\n    \"createSurface\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"celestial-express-mystery\",\n      \"catalogId\": \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\",\n      \"theme\": {\n        \"primaryColor\": \"#1A237E\",\n        \"agentDisplayName\": \"Mystery Writer\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"version\": \"v0.9\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"updateComponents\": {\n      \"surfaceId\": \"celestial-express-mystery\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"root\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"header_title\",\n            \"assumptions_text\",\n            \"divider_1\",\n            \"section_setting_title\",\n            \"section_setting_body\",\n            \"section_victim_title\",\n            \"section_victim_body\",\n            \"section_weapon_title\",\n            \"section_weapon_body\",\n            \"section_susp