uesday (90 min): Rates and Work Problems.\n- Wednesday (90 min): General review of all Arithmetic topics covered.\n- Thursday (90 min): Take a 30-40 minute timed quiz on Arithmetic. Spend the remaining time reviewing every mistake.\n\nWeek 2: Algebra (August 2 - August 8)\n- Friday (90 min): Operations with Algebraic Expressions, Rules of Exponents.\n- Saturday (3 hrs): Solving Linear & Quadratic Equations, Systems of Equations, and Inequalities. Focus on word problems that translate to algebraic equations.\n- Monday (90 min): Functions and their properties (f(x) notation, domain, range).\n- Tuesday (90 min): Advanced Word Problems (mixture, interest, etc.).\n- Wednesday (90 min): General review of all Algebra topics.\n- Thursday (90 min): Take a 30-40 minute timed quiz on Algebra. Spend the remaining time on detailed error analysis.\n\nWeek 3: Geometry (August 9 - August 15)\n- Friday (90 min): Lines, Angles, Triangles, and Quadrilaterals. Memorize key formulas.\n- Saturday (3 hrs): Circles, Polygons, and 3D Figures (Cubes, Cylinders). Practice problems involving combined shapes.\n- Monday (90 min): Coordinate Geometry (Slope, Intercepts, Distance Formula, Midpoint).\n- Tuesday (90 min): Mixed Geometry problem-solving session.\n- Wednesday (90 min): General review of all Geometry topics and formulas.\n- Thursday (90 min): Take a 30-40 minute timed quiz on Geometry. Review all mistakes and the underlying formulas.\n\nWeek 4: Data Analysis (August 16 - August 22)\n- Friday (90 min): Statistics (Mean, Median, Mode, Range).\n- Saturday (3 hrs): Advanced Statistics (Standard Deviation, Quartiles, Percentiles) and Probability.\n- Monday (90 min): Combinatorics (Permutations and Combinations).\n- Tuesday (90 min): Data Interpretation (Graphs, Charts, Tables). Focus on reading and extracting information quickly.\n- Wednesday (90 min): General review of all Data Analysis topics.\n- Thursday (90 min): Take a 30-40 minute timed quiz on Data Analysis. Review errors thoroughly.