rs much more comfortable temperatures, while Bangkok guarantees brighter photography conditions at the cost of heat exhaustion risks.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"id\": \"historical_data_heading\",\n          \"text\": \"Historical Data Context\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"id\": \"historical_data_p1\",\n          \"text\": \"The following comparison relies on historical climate averages collected over the last 30 years. January weather patterns in Southeast Asia are generally stable, but short-term fluctuations (such as cold snaps in Hanoi or heatwaves in Bangkok) can occur.\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"id\": \"historical_data_p2\",\n          \"text\": \"\\\"Rainfall probability\\\" here refers to the likelihood of measurable precipitation days, though intensity varies (Bangkok rain is rare/short; Hanoi rain is often a persistent light drizzle).\",\n          \"variant\": \"body\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"id\": \"weather_metrics_heading\",\n          \"text\": \"Bangkok vs Hanoi Weather Metrics\",\n          \"variant\": \"h2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"List\",\n          \"id\": \"weather_table\",\n          \"direction\": \"vertical\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"table_header_row\",\n            \"table_divider_1\",\n            \"temp_row\",\n            \"table_divider_2\",\n            \"humidity_row\",\n            \"table_divider_3\",\n            \"rain_row\",\n            \"table_divider_4\",\n            \"sky_row\",\n            \"table_divider_5\",\n            \"walking_row\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"component\": \"Row\",\n          \"id\": \"table_header_row\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"header_fea