deception_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"deception_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"deception_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\": [\n            \"deception_title\",\n            \"deception_description\",\n            \"deception_bgg_button\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"deception_title\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"Option 3: Deception: Murder in Hong Kong | Crime-solving deduction game | Social Deduction / 20 Minutes\",\n          \"variant\": \"h4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"deception_description\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"One player is secretly the Murderer, and another is the Forensic Scientist who knows the solution but can only communicate by placing markers on scene tiles (like Cause of Death: Suffocation). The remaining players are investigators trying to interpret these vague clues to identify the murderer and the weapon used. It is less aggressive than other lying games because the focus is on the evidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"deception_bgg_button\",\n          \"component\": \"Button\",\n          \"child\": \"deception_bgg_button_text\",\n          \"action\": {\n            \"functionCall\": {\n              \"call\": \"openUrl\",\n              \"args\": {\n                \"url\": \"https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/156129/deception-murder-in-hong-kong\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"deception_bgg_button_text\",\n          \"component\": \"Text\",\n          \"text\": \"View on BoardGameGeek\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"resistance_card\",\n          \"component\": \"Card\",\n          \"child\": \"resistance_content\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"resistance_content\",\n          \"component\": \"Column\",\n          \"children\"